{
 "theorem_quoted": "UPPER_BOUND.md Section 7, paragraph after (31): using (SW) with q=1, for every fixed H, max_{t<=N}|Delta(t)| <<_H N L^{-H}, and (29) only gives T_N <<_H N^3 L^{-2H}, where T_N = sum_{t=1}^{N} Delta(t)^2 + sum_{t=1}^{N-1} [Delta(N)-Delta(t)]^2 and L = log N. Proved from (SW) (Siegel-Walfisz) alone: 'No RH estimate is used in (1), (13), (26), (29), or (30).'",
 "what_is_compared": "delta_sq_probe.py measures S(N) = sum_{t=1}^{N} Delta(t)^2, the leading of T_N's two non-negative summands, not T_N itself; the second summand, sum_{t=1}^{N-1} [Delta(N)-Delta(t)]^2, is not measured anywhere in this hunt. Because both summands are sums of squares, S(N) <= T_N for every N, so a convention-bound exceeded by measured S(N) is also exceeded by T_N, but a convention-bound that exceeds measured S(N) says nothing about whether it would still exceed T_N, since the unmeasured second summand could push T_N past it.",
 "source_measured_S_N": "hunts/prime_pair_error/results_delta_sq.json, key 'rows'",
